nating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. Use when the user wants to review a branch, a PR, work-in-progress changes, or asks to \"review since X\".", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/code-review", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"codebase-design", Name:"codebase-design", Description:"Shared vocabulary for designing deep modules. Use when the user wants to design or improve a module's interface, find deepening opportunities, decide where a seam goes, make code more testable or AI-navigable, or when another skill needs the deep-module vocabulary.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/codebase-design", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"computer-use", Name:"computer-use", Description:"Drive a macOS app through the `computer` tool — read its accessibility tree, act on elements, and use real input only when the tree cannot reach the target.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/computer-use", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"design-taste-frontend", Name:"design-taste-frontend", Description:"Anti-slop frontend skill for landing pages, portfolios, and redesigns. The agent reads the brief, infers the right design direction, and ships interfaces that do not look templated. Real design systems when applicable, audit-first on redesigns, strict pre-flight check.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"design-taste-frontend-v1", Name:"design-taste-frontend-v1", Description:"The original v1 taste-skill, preserved for projects depending on its exact behavior. The current default is `design-taste-frontend` (v2 experimental), which is a substantial rewrite. Use this v1 install name only if you need exact backward compatibility.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend-v1", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"diagnosing-bugs", Name:"diagnosing-bugs", Description:"Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says \"diagnose\"/\"debug this\", or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/diagnosing-bugs", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"domain-modeling", Name:"domain-modeling", Description:"Build and sharpen a project's domain model. Use when discussing codebase terminology, writing or editing a CONTEXT.md, or recording or editing an ADR.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/domain-modeling", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"full-output-enforcement", Name:"full-output-enforcement", Description:"Overrides default LLM truncation behavior. Enforces complete code generation, bans placeholder patterns, and handles token-limit splits cleanly. Apply to any task requiring exhaustive, unabridged output.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/full-output-enforcement", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"git-guardrails-claude-code", Name:"git-guardrails-claude-code", Description:"Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/git-guardrails-claude-code", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"gpt-taste", Name:"gpt-taste", Description:"Elite UX/UI & Advanced GSAP Motion Engineer. Enforces Python-driven true randomization for layout variance, strict AIDA page structure, wide editorial typography (bans 6-line wraps), gapless bento grids, strict GSAP ScrollTriggers (pinning, stacking, scrubbing), inline micro-images, and massive section spacing.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/gpt-taste", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"graphify", Name:"graphify-windows", Description:"Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/graphify", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:9}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grill-me", Name:"grill-me", Description:"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/grill-me", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grill-with-docs", Name:"grill-with-docs", Description:"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design, which also creates docs (ADR's and glossary) as we go.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/grill-with-docs", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grilling", Name:"grilling", Description:"Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any 'grill' trigger phrases.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/grilling", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"handoff", Name:"handoff", Description:"Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/handoff", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"high-end-visual-design", Name:"high-end-visual-design", Description:"Teaches the AI to design like a high-end agency. Defines the exact fonts, spacing, shadows, card structures, and animations that make a website feel expensive. Blocks all the common defaults that make AI designs look cheap or generic.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/high-end-visual-design", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"image-to-code", Name:"image-to-code", Description:"Elite website image-to-code skill for Codex. For visually important web tasks, it must first generate the design image(s) itself, deeply analyze them, then implement the website to match them as closely as possible. In Codex, it must prefer large, readable, section-specific images instead of tiny compressed boards, generate fresh standalone images for sections or detail views instead of cropping old ones, avoid lazy under-generation, avoid cards-inside-cards-inside-cards UI, and keep the hero clean, spacious, readable, and visible on a small laptop.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/image-to-code", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"imagegen-frontend-mobile", Name:"imagegen-frontend-mobile", Description:"Elite mobile app image-generation skill for creating premium, app-native screen concepts and flows. Designed for iOS, Android, and cross-platform mobile products. Prioritizes clean hierarchy, comfortably readable text, strong multi-screen consistency, controlled color palettes, non-generic creative direction, textured surfaces, image-led composition, tasteful custom iconography, and clean phone mockup framing. By default, screens should be shown inside a subtle premium iPhone or similar phone mockup with a visible frame, while the main focus stays on the app content itself. This skill generates images only. It does not write code.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"imagegen-frontend-web", Name:"imagegen-frontend-web", Description:"Elite frontend image-direction skill for generating premium, conversion-aware website design references. CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — generate ONE separate horizontal image FOR EVERY section. A landing page with 8 sections produces 8 images. Never compress multiple sections into one image. Enforces composition variety (not always left-text / right-image), background-image freedom, varied CTAs, varied hero scales (giant / mid / mini minimalist), narrative concept spine, second-read moments, and a single consistent palette across all images. Optimized for landing pages, marketing sites, and product comps that developers or coding models can accurately recreate.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-web", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"implement", Name:"implement", Description:"Implement a piece of work based on a spec or set of tickets.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/implement", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"implement-spec", Name:"implement-spec", Description:"Implement a specification in code.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/implement-spec", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"improve-codebase-architecture", Name:"improve-codebase-architecture", Description:"Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/improve-codebase-architecture", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"industrial-brutalist-ui", Name:"industrial-brutalist-ui", Description:"Raw mechanical interfaces fusing Swiss typographic print with military terminal aesthetics. Rigid grids, extreme type scale contrast, utilitarian color, analog degradation effects. For data-heavy dashboards, portfolios, or editorial sites that need to feel like declassified blueprints.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"jev-ultrafast", Name:"jev-ultrafast", Description:"", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/jev-ultrafast", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"karpathy-guidelines", Name:"karpathy-guidelines", Description:"Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring code to avoid overcomplication, make surgical changes, surface assumptions, and define verifiable success criteria.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/karpathy-guidelines", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"loop-me", Name:"loop-me", Description:"Grill me about specs for the workflows I want to build, within this workspace.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/loop-me", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"migrate-to-shoehorn", Name:"migrate-to-shoehorn", Description:"Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/migrate-to-shoehorn", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"minimalist-ui", Name:"minimalist-ui", Description:"Clean editorial-style interfaces. Warm monochrome palette, typographic contrast, flat bento grids, muted pastels. No gradients, no heavy shadows.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/minimalist-ui", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail", Name:"ponytail", Description:"Forces the laziest solution that actually works, simplest, shortest, most minimal. Channels a senior dev who has seen everything: question whether the task needs to exist at all (YAGNI), reach for the standard library before custom code, native platform features before dependencies, one line before fifty. Supports intensity levels: lite, full (default), ultra. Use on ANY coding task: writing, adding, refactoring, fixing, reviewing, or designing code, and choosing libraries or dependencies. Also use whenever the user says \"ponytail\", \"be lazy\", \"lazy mode\", \"simplest solution\", \"minimal solution\", \"yagni\", \"do less\", or \"shortest path\", or complains about over-engineering, bloat, boilerplate, or unnecessary dependencies. Do NOT use for non-coding requests (general knowledge, prose, translation, summaries, recipes).", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail-audit", Name:"ponytail-audit", Description:"Whole-repo audit for over-engineering. Like ponytail-review, but scans the entire codebase instead of a diff: a ranked list of what to delete, simplify, or replace with stdlib/native equivalents. Use when the user says \"audit this codebase\", \"audit for over-engineering\", \"what can I delete from this repo\", \"find bloat\", \"ponytail-audit\", or \"/ponytail-audit\". One-shot report, does not apply fixes.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail-audit", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail-debt", Name:"ponytail-debt", Description:"Harvest every `ponytail:` comment in the codebase into a debt ledger, so the deliberate shortcuts and deferrals ponytail leaves behind get tracked instead of rotting into \"later means never\". Use when the user says \"ponytail debt\", \"/ponytail-debt\", \"what did ponytail defer\", \"list the shortcuts\", \"ponytail ledger\", or \"what did we mark to do later\". One-shot report, changes nothing.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail-debt", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail-gain", Name:"ponytail-gain", Description:"Show ponytail's measured impact as a compact scoreboard: less code, less cost, more speed, from the benchmark medians. One-shot display, not a persistent mode, and not a per-repo number. Trigger: /ponytail-gain, \"ponytail gain\", \"what does ponytail save\", \"show ponytail impact\", \"ponytail scoreboard\".", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail-gain", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail-help", Name:"ponytail-help", Description:"Quick-reference card for all ponytail modes, skills, and commands. One-shot display, not a persistent mode. Trigger: /ponytail-help, \"ponytail help\", \"what ponytail commands\", \"how do I use ponytail\".", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail-help", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"ponytail-review", Name:"ponytail-review", Description:"Code review focused exclusively on over-engineering. Finds what to delete: reinvented standard library, unneeded dependencies, speculative abstractions, dead flexibility. One line per finding: location, what to cut, what replaces it. Use when the user says \"review for over-engineering\", \"what can we delete\", \"is this over-engineered\", \"simplify review\", or invokes /ponytail-review. Complements correctness-focused review, this one only hunts complexity.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/ponytail-review", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"prototype", Name:"prototype", Description:"Build a throwaway prototype to answer a design question. Use when the user wants to sanity-check whether a state model or logic feels right, or explore what a UI should look like.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/prototype", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"redesign-existing-projects", Name:"redesign-existing-projects", Description:"Upgrades existing websites and apps to premium quality. Audits current design, identifies generic AI patterns, and applies high-end design standards without breaking functionality. Works with any CSS framework or vanilla CSS.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/redesign-existing-projects", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"research", Name:"research", Description:"Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/research", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"resolving-merge-conflicts", Name:"resolving-merge-conflicts", Description:"Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/resolving-merge-conflicts", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"retro", Name:"retro", Description:"Conduct a retrospective on a coding session.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/retro", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"scaffold-exercises", Name:"scaffold-exercises", Description:"Create exercise directory structures with sections, problems, solutions, and explainers that pass linting. Use when user wants to scaffold exercises, create exercise stubs, or set up a new course section.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/scaffold-exercises", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"semantic-compression", Name:"semantic-compression", Description:"Re-encode verbose prose into a dense telegraphic register — punctuation as connectives, label frames, verbless assertions — without losing normativity or precision. Use when compressing system prompts, tool/function descriptions, skill bodies, or agent instructions; reducing token count or context bloat; making documentation token-efficient for LLM input; or rewriting text in compressed notation.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/semantic-compression", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"setup-matt-pocock-skills", Name:"setup-matt-pocock-skills", Description:"Configure this repo for the engineering skills: set up its issue tracker, triage label vocabulary, and domain doc layout. Run once before first use of the other engineering skills.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/setup-matt-pocock-skills", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"setup-pre-commit", Name:"setup-pre-commit", Description:"Set up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged (Prettier), type checking, and tests in the current repo. Use when user wants to add pre-commit hooks, set up Husky, configure lint-staged, or add commit-time formatting/typechecking/testing.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/setup-pre-commit", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"setup-ts-deep-modules", Name:"setup-ts-deep-modules", Description:"Wire dependency-cruiser into a TypeScript repo so each package is a deep module, with implementation hidden in subfolders and reachable only through its entry-point files. User-invoked.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/setup-ts-deep-modules", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"stitch-design-taste", Name:"stitch-design-taste", Description:"Semantic Design System Skill for Google Stitch. Generates agent-friendly DESIGN.md files that enforce premium, anti-generic UI standards — strict typography, calibrated color, asymmetric layouts, perpetual micro-motion, and hardware-accelerated performance.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/stitch-design-taste", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:2}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"system-prompts", Name:"system-prompts", Description:"Write system prompts, tool docs, and agent definitions. Project tag conventions + RFC 2119 keywords + dense compression. Use when authoring or editing any prompt the model reads.", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/system-prompts", Provider:"mcode", Root:"universal", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:2}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"systematic-debugging", Name:"systematic-debugging", Description:"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/systematic-debugging", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"tavily-search", Name:"tavily-search", Description:"Search the web with LLM-optimized results via the Tavily CLI. Use this skill when the user wants to search the web, find articles, look up information, get recent news, discover sources, or says \"search for\", \"find me\", \"look up\", \"what's the latest on\", \"find articles about\", or needs current information from the internet. Returns relevant results with content snippets, relevance scores, and metadata — optimized for LLM consumption. Supports domain filtering, time ranges, and multiple search depths.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/tavily-search", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"tdd", Name:"tdd", Description:"Test-driven development. Use when the user wants to build features or fix bugs test-first, mentions \"red-green-refactor\", or wants integration tests.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/tdd", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"teach", Name:"teach", Description:"Teach the user a new skill or concept, within this workspace.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/teach", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"to-questionnaire", Name:"to-questionnaire", Description:"Turn a decision you can't fully answer into a questionnaire for someone else to fill in.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/to-questionnaire", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"to-spec", Name:"to-spec", Description:"Turn the current conversation into a spec and publish it to the project issue tracker: no interview, just synthesis of what you've already discussed.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/to-spec", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"to-tickets", Name:"to-tickets", Description:"Break a plan, spec, or the current conversation into a set of tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its blocking edges, published to the configured tracker (edges as text in one file per ticket locally, or native blocking links on a real tracker).", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/to-tickets", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"triage", Name:"triage", Description:"Move issues and external PRs through a state machine of triage roles, categorise, verify, grill if needed, and write agent-ready briefs.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/triage", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"wait-what", Name:"wait-what", Description:"Stop. That last message did not land: re-pitch it.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/wait-what", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"wayfinder", Name:"wayfinder", Description:"Plan a huge chunk of work (more than one agent session can hold) as a shared map of decision tickets on your issue tracker, and resolve them one at a time until the way to the destination is clear.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/wayfinder", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"wizard", Name:"wizard", Description:"Generate an interactive bash wizard that walks a human through steps only they can perform. Use when provisioning infrastructure, setting up credentials or CI secrets, walking an unfamiliar third-party dashboard, or running a one-off migration or cutover. Don't invoke this for steps the agent can perform itself.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/wizard", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"writing-beats", Name:"writing-beats", Description:"Writing, exploit; assemble raw material into a journey of beats, grounding each term before a beat leans on it.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/writing-beats", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"writing-for-agents", Name:"writing-for-agents", Description:"Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/writing-for-agents", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"writing-fragments", Name:"writing-fragments", Description:"Writing, explore: mine raw fragments, no structure yet.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/writing-fragments", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"writing-plans", Name:"writing-plans", Description:"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/writing-plans", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"writing-shape", Name:"writing-shape", Description:"Writing, exploit: shape raw material into an article, paragraph by paragraph.", SourcePath:"~/.minimax/skills/writing-shape", Provider:"mcode", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:false, FileCount:1}}
