    local_skills_test.go:556: expected only GROK_HOME skill, got [{Key:ask-matt Name:ask-matt Description:Ask which skill or flow fits your situation. A router over the skills in this repo. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ask-matt Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:3} {Key:brandkit Name:brandkit Description:Premium brand-kit image generation skill for creating high-end brand-guidelines boards, logo systems, identity decks, and visual-world presentations. Trained for minimalist, cinematic, editorial, dark-tech, luxury, cultural, security, gaming, developer-tool, and consumer-app brand systems. Optimized for intentional logo concepting, refined composition, sparse typography, strong symbolic meaning, premium mockups, art-directed imagery, and flexible grid layouts. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/brandkit Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:browser-use Name:browser-use Description:Drive the in-app browser — open a page, read it as an accessibility tree, click, type, fill forms, screenshot, and verify what the page really shows. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/browser-use Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:claude-handoff Name:claude-handoff Description:Hand the current conversation off to a fresh background agent that picks up the work immediately. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/claude-handoff Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:code-review Name:code-review Description:Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. Use when the user wants to review a branch, a PR, work-in-progress changes, or asks to "review since X". SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/code-review Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:codebase-design Name:codebase-design Description:Shared vocabulary for designing deep modules. Use when the user wants to design or improve a module's interface, find deepening opportunities, decide where a seam goes, make code more testable or AI-navigable, or when another skill needs the deep-module vocabulary. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/codebase-design Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:4} {Key:computer-use Name:computer-use Description:Drive a macOS app through the `computer` tool — read its accessibility tree, act on elements, and use real input only when the tree cannot reach the target. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/computer-use Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:design-taste-frontend Name:design-taste-frontend Description:Anti-slop frontend skill for landing pages, portfolios, and redesigns. The agent reads the brief, infers the right design direction, and ships interfaces that do not look templated. Real design systems when applicable, audit-first on redesigns, strict pre-flight check. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:design-taste-frontend-v1 Name:design-taste-frontend-v1 Description:The original v1 taste-skill, preserved for projects depending on its exact behavior. The current default is `design-taste-frontend` (v2 experimental), which is a substantial rewrite. Use this v1 install name only if you need exact backward compatibility. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend-v1 Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:diagnosing-bugs Name:diagnosing-bugs Description:Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says "diagnose"/"debug this", or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/diagnosing-bugs Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:3} {Key:domain-modeling Name:domain-modeling Description:Build and sharpen a project's domain model. Use when discussing codebase terminology, writing or editing a CONTEXT.md, or recording or editing an ADR. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/domain-modeling Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:4} {Key:full-output-enforcement Name:full-output-enforcement Description:Overrides default LLM truncation behavior. Enforces complete code generation, bans placeholder patterns, and handles token-limit splits cleanly. Apply to any task requiring exhaustive, unabridged output. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/full-output-enforcement Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:git-guardrails-claude-code Name:git-guardrails-claude-code Description:Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/git-guardrails-claude-code Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:3} {Key:gpt-taste Name:gpt-taste Description:Elite UX/UI & Advanced GSAP Motion Engineer. Enforces Python-driven true randomization for layout variance, strict AIDA page structure, wide editorial typography (bans 6-line wraps), gapless bento grids, strict GSAP ScrollTriggers (pinning, stacking, scrubbing), inline micro-images, and massive section spacing. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/gpt-taste Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:graphify Name:graphify-windows Description:Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/graphify Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:9} {Key:grill-me Name:grill-me Description:A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/grill-me Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:grill-with-docs Name:grill-with-docs Description:A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design, which also creates docs (ADR's and glossary) as we go. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/grill-with-docs Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:grilling Name:grilling Description:Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any 'grill' trigger phrases. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/grilling Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:handoff Name:handoff Description:Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/handoff Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:high-end-visual-design Name:high-end-visual-design Description:Teaches the AI to design like a high-end agency. Defines the exact fonts, spacing, shadows, card structures, and animations that make a website feel expensive. Blocks all the common defaults that make AI designs look cheap or generic. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/high-end-visual-design Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:image-to-code Name:image-to-code Description:Elite website image-to-code skill for Codex. For visually important web tasks, it must first generate the design image(s) itself, deeply analyze them, then implement the website to match them as closely as possible. In Codex, it must prefer large, readable, section-specific images instead of tiny compressed boards, generate fresh standalone images for sections or detail views instead of cropping old ones, avoid lazy under-generation, avoid cards-inside-cards-inside-cards UI, and keep the hero clean, spacious, readable, and visible on a small laptop. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/image-to-code Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:imagegen-frontend-mobile Name:imagegen-frontend-mobile Description:Elite mobile app image-generation skill for creating premium, app-native screen concepts and flows. Designed for iOS, Android, and cross-platform mobile products. Prioritizes clean hierarchy, comfortably readable text, strong multi-screen consistency, controlled color palettes, non-generic creative direction, textured surfaces, image-led composition, tasteful custom iconography, and clean phone mockup framing. By default, screens should be shown inside a subtle premium iPhone or similar phone mockup with a visible frame, while the main focus stays on the app content itself. This skill generates images only. It does not write code. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:imagegen-frontend-web Name:imagegen-frontend-web Description:Elite frontend image-direction skill for generating premium, conversion-aware website design references. CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — generate ONE separate horizontal image FOR EVERY section. A landing page with 8 sections produces 8 images. Never compress multiple sections into one image. Enforces composition variety (not always left-text / right-image), background-image freedom, varied CTAs, varied hero scales (giant / mid / mini minimalist), narrative concept spine, second-read moments, and a single consistent palette across all images. Optimized for landing pages, marketing sites, and product comps that developers or coding models can accurately recreate. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-web Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:implement Name:implement Description:Implement a piece of work based on a spec or set of tickets. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/implement Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:implement-spec Name:implement-spec Description:Implement a specification in code. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/implement-spec Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:improve-codebase-architecture Name:improve-codebase-architecture Description:Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/improve-codebase-architecture Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:3} {Key:industrial-brutalist-ui Name:industrial-brutalist-ui Description:Raw mechanical interfaces fusing Swiss typographic print with military terminal aesthetics. Rigid grids, extreme type scale contrast, utilitarian color, analog degradation effects. For data-heavy dashboards, portfolios, or editorial sites that need to feel like declassified blueprints. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:jev-ultrafast Name:jev-ultrafast Description: SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/jev-ultrafast Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:karpathy-guidelines Name:karpathy-guidelines Description:Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring code to avoid overcomplication, make surgical changes, surface assumptions, and define verifiable success criteria. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/karpathy-guidelines Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:loop-me Name:loop-me Description:Grill me about specs for the workflows I want to build, within this workspace. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/loop-me Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:migrate-to-shoehorn Name:migrate-to-shoehorn Description:Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/migrate-to-shoehorn Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:minimalist-ui Name:minimalist-ui Description:Clean editorial-style interfaces. Warm monochrome palette, typographic contrast, flat bento grids, muted pastels. No gradients, no heavy shadows. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/minimalist-ui Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail Name:ponytail Description:Forces the laziest solution that actually works, simplest, shortest, most minimal. Channels a senior dev who has seen everything: question whether the task needs to exist at all (YAGNI), reach for the standard library before custom code, native platform features before dependencies, one line before fifty. Supports intensity levels: lite, full (default), ultra. Use on ANY coding task: writing, adding, refactoring, fixing, reviewing, or designing code, and choosing libraries or dependencies. Also use whenever the user says "ponytail", "be lazy", "lazy mode", "simplest solution", "minimal solution", "yagni", "do less", or "shortest path", or complains about over-engineering, bloat, boilerplate, or unnecessary dependencies. Do NOT use for non-coding requests (general knowledge, prose, translation, summaries, recipes). SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-audit Name:ponytail-audit Description:Whole-repo audit for over-engineering. Like ponytail-review, but scans the entire codebase instead of a diff: a ranked list of what to delete, simplify, or replace with stdlib/native equivalents. Use when the user says "audit this codebase", "audit for over-engineering", "what can I delete from this repo", "find bloat", "ponytail-audit", or "/ponytail-audit". One-shot report, does not apply fixes. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail-audit Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-debt Name:ponytail-debt Description:Harvest every `ponytail:` comment in the codebase into a debt ledger, so the deliberate shortcuts and deferrals ponytail leaves behind get tracked instead of rotting into "later means never". Use when the user says "ponytail debt", "/ponytail-debt", "what did ponytail defer", "list the shortcuts", "ponytail ledger", or "what did we mark to do later". One-shot report, changes nothing. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail-debt Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-gain Name:ponytail-gain Description:Show ponytail's measured impact as a compact scoreboard: less code, less cost, more speed, from the benchmark medians. One-shot display, not a persistent mode, and not a per-repo number. Trigger: /ponytail-gain, "ponytail gain", "what does ponytail save", "show ponytail impact", "ponytail scoreboard". SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail-gain Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-help Name:ponytail-help Description:Quick-reference card for all ponytail modes, skills, and commands. One-shot display, not a persistent mode. Trigger: /ponytail-help, "ponytail help", "what ponytail commands", "how do I use ponytail". SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail-help Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-review Name:ponytail-review Description:Code review focused exclusively on over-engineering. Finds what to delete: reinvented standard library, unneeded dependencies, speculative abstractions, dead flexibility. One line per finding: location, what to cut, what replaces it. Use when the user says "review for over-engineering", "what can we delete", "is this over-engineered", "simplify review", or invokes /ponytail-review. Complements correctness-focused review, this one only hunts complexity. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail-review Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:prototype Name:prototype Description:Build a throwaway prototype to answer a design question. Use when the user wants to sanity-check whether a state model or logic feels right, or explore what a UI should look like. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/prototype Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:4} {Key:redesign-existing-projects Name:redesign-existing-projects Description:Upgrades existing websites and apps to premium quality. Audits current design, identifies generic AI patterns, and applies high-end design standards without breaking functionality. Works with any CSS framework or vanilla CSS. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/redesign-existing-projects Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:research Name:research Description:Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/research Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:resolving-merge-conflicts Name:resolving-merge-conflicts Description:Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/resolving-merge-conflicts Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:retro Name:retro Description:Conduct a retrospective on a coding session. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/retro Provider:grok Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:review-helper Name:Grok Home Review Description:Review code SourcePath:~/AppData/Local/Temp/multica-task-2074477066/TestListRuntimeLocalSkills_GrokUsesGROKHOME442154325/002/custom-grok-home/skills/review-helper Provider:grok Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:scaffold-exercises Name:scaffold-exercises 