azy under-generation, avoid cards-inside-cards-inside-cards UI, and keep the hero clean, spacious, readable, and visible on a small laptop. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/image-to-code Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:imagegen-frontend-mobile Name:imagegen-frontend-mobile Description:Elite mobile app image-generation skill for creating premium, app-native screen concepts and flows. Designed for iOS, Android, and cross-platform mobile products. Prioritizes clean hierarchy, comfortably readable text, strong multi-screen consistency, controlled color palettes, non-generic creative direction, textured surfaces, image-led composition, tasteful custom iconography, and clean phone mockup framing. By default, screens should be shown inside a subtle premium iPhone or similar phone mockup with a visible frame, while the main focus stays on the app content itself. This skill generates images only. It does not write code. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:imagegen-frontend-web Name:imagegen-frontend-web Description:Elite frontend image-direction skill for generating premium, conversion-aware website design references. CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — generate ONE separate horizontal image FOR EVERY section. A landing page with 8 sections produces 8 images. Never compress multiple sections into one image. Enforces composition variety (not always left-text / right-image), background-image freedom, varied CTAs, varied hero scales (giant / mid / mini minimalist), narrative concept spine, second-read moments, and a single consistent palette across all images. Optimized for landing pages, marketing sites, and product comps that developers or coding models can accurately recreate. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/imagegen-frontend-web Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:implement Name:implement Description:Implement a piece of work based on a spec or set of tickets. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/implement Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:implement-spec Name:implement-spec Description:Implement a specification in code. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/implement-spec Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:improve-codebase-architecture Name:improve-codebase-architecture Description:Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/improve-codebase-architecture Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:3} {Key:industrial-brutalist-ui Name:industrial-brutalist-ui Description:Raw mechanical interfaces fusing Swiss typographic print with military terminal aesthetics. Rigid grids, extreme type scale contrast, utilitarian color, analog degradation effects. For data-heavy dashboards, portfolios, or editorial sites that need to feel like declassified blueprints. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:jev-ultrafast Name:jev-ultrafast Description: SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/jev-ultrafast Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:karpathy-guidelines Name:karpathy-guidelines Description:Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring code to avoid overcomplication, make surgical changes, surface assumptions, and define verifiable success criteria. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/karpathy-guidelines Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:loop-me Name:loop-me Description:Grill me about specs for the workflows I want to build, within this workspace. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/loop-me Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:migrate-to-shoehorn Name:migrate-to-shoehorn Description:Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/migrate-to-shoehorn Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:minimalist-ui Name:minimalist-ui Description:Clean editorial-style interfaces. Warm monochrome palette, typographic contrast, flat bento grids, muted pastels. No gradients, no heavy shadows. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/minimalist-ui Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail Name:ponytail Description:Forces the laziest solution that actually works, simplest, shortest, most minimal. Channels a senior dev who has seen everything: question whether the task needs to exist at all (YAGNI), reach for the standard library before custom code, native platform features before dependencies, one line before fifty. Supports intensity levels: lite, full (default), ultra. Use on ANY coding task: writing, adding, refactoring, fixing, reviewing, or designing code, and choosing libraries or dependencies. Also use whenever the user says "ponytail", "be lazy", "lazy mode", "simplest solution", "minimal solution", "yagni", "do less", or "shortest path", or complains about over-engineering, bloat, boilerplate, or unnecessary dependencies. Do NOT use for non-coding requests (general knowledge, prose, translation, summaries, recipes). SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/ponytail Provider:qwen Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:ponytail-audit Name:ponytail-audit Description:Whole-repo audit for over-engineering. Like ponytail-review, but scans the entire codebase instead of a diff: a ranked list of what to delete, simplify, or replace with stdlib/native equivalents. Use when the user says "audit this codebase", "audit for over-engineering", "what can I delete from this repo", "find bloat", "ponytail-audit", or "/ponytail-audit". One-shot report, does not apply fixes. SourcePath